(7455387, 1180962, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Congrats on the top ten finish, Georges, don''t know why it didn''t score higher.  Still, 8th place is nothing to scoff at.  Love the energy of the leashed dog bounding at the trepidatious dog on the right, who though at liberty is playing it safe and styuing out of way of any potential harm!  I also really like the legs and flowered dress of the woman owner of the white dog, there is something so grounding in that element that it adds a lot to the pic.  So does the shadow of the dog on the right.<br/> <br/>The high ISO is unavoidable, lucky for you Canon has enviable noise control so though I can see it, there aren''t huge disruptive chunks of it floating around.  The existing textures of the scene help to camouflage it nicely.<br/> <br/>Overall a very well-seen and well-caught shot, you should be proud of it!  Keep up the good work.<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Congrats on the top ten finish, Georges, don''t know why it didn''t score higher.  Still, 8th place is nothing to scoff at.  Love the energy of the leashed dog bounding at the trepidatious dog on the right, who though at liberty is playing it safe and styuing out of way of any potential harm!  I also really like the legs and flowered dress of the woman owner of the white dog, there is something so grounding in that element that it adds a lot to the pic.  So does the shadow of the dog on the right. The high ISO is unavoidable, lucky for you Canon has enviable noise control so though I can see it, there aren''t huge disruptive chunks of it floating around.  The existing textures of the scene help to camouflage it nicely. Overall a very well-seen and well-caught shot, you should be proud of it!  Keep up the good work. Susan', '2016-05-18 21:37:59.000000', NULL, 0),
